Scope

The MIT License above covers Horizont: the code, the design tokens, the CSS,
the Hugo partials and shortcodes, the tools, the documentation and the
graphics drawn for Horizont (UI symbols, device frames, illustrations), unless
listed below. Paths are relative to the root of the repository
github.com/regetskcob/horizont.

Not covered by the MIT License:

1. Fonts. They keep their own licences, whose full texts ship next to them:

   - Literata, Mona Sans (with Mona Sans Display Expanded) and Monaspace
     Argon, in flutter/fonts/ and web/fonts/: SIL Open Font License 1.1,
     see flutter/fonts/OFL.txt and web/fonts/OFL.txt.
   - Material Symbols Sharp, as a subset in
     flutter/fonts/MaterialSymbolsSharp-300.ttf and
     web/fonts/MaterialSymbols/MaterialSymbolsSharp-300.woff2: Apache
     License 2.0, see flutter/fonts/MaterialSymbols-LICENSE.txt and
     web/fonts/MaterialSymbols/LICENSE.txt. The symbols Horizont draws itself
     and adds to that subset (codepoints from U+100000) are also available
     under the MIT License in their source form, icons/symbols/*.svg.

2. Product marks and names. The marks, app icons and names of regetskcob,
   Jagdaufseher, KNX Monitor, Panzergefecht, Kalkar IT Solutions and Kalkar
   Kompakt identify these products and are not licensed for other products.
   This covers the drawings in web/partials/mark.html and
   web/partials/app-icon.html, their sources in icons/svg/ and the exported
   sets in icons/export/. You may show them to refer to these products. All
   other rights reserved.

3. The Flutter logo in the showcase app (flutter/example/web/favicon.png,
   flutter/example/web/icons/, flutter/example/macos/Runner/Assets.xcassets/
   AppIcon.appiconset/). It comes from the Flutter app template and is a
   trademark of Google LLC.
